     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I want to say thank you and renjin shows much potential.<div>I understand that this package (prodlim) has errors  according to <a href=\"http://packages.renjin.org/packages/prodlim.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://packages.renjin.org/packages/prodlim.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793344124092000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3sHZDWvnYxIG3rmFYadx0s\">http://packages.renjin.org/packages/prodlim.html</a>, but would like to integrate it.<div><div>I read many of the docs, is there an example of how to do integrate an cran package from r to renjin?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>-Jim</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>The entire class appears to be missing</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"padding:9.5px;font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;color:rgb(51,51,51);border-top-left-radius:4px;border-top-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-left-radius:4px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:20px;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.14902);background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\">org.renjin.cran.prodlim.prodlim</pre></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
